  "implementation": [
    "Legacy finite login Host startBrowser only: original AnalyzeUrl GET URL/headers, current task/source binding and deadline, source.browser checked receipt.",
    "Existing Presenter queue displays JsBridgeBrowserView with sourceRunHandler=nil, preserving sole Rhino evaluator and existing CookieStore owner.",
    "Real UIKit completion followed by authorization checks is the only presentation success ACK. Before/during cancellation or admission failure retracts page, keeps issued-side-effect status and prevents later JS writes.",
    "Accepted nonawait page outlives normal producer/session/revoke cleanup. Existing UI then owns Cookie capture, which is not claimed as this original task committed Cookie effects.",
    "Async explicit cancel waits for actual UIKit dismissal callback. New original page uses overFullScreen to keep underlying form mounted; no fixed delay, extra store/VM/global UI adapter."
  ],
  "validationHistory": [
    "First direct production compile succeeded. Validation-only ownership assertion then rejected7 nested inline classes whose SourceFile reports RuleCompat.kt; corrected to bind actual outer class roots plus SourceFile, preserved script/log, no production recompile.",
    "First javac rejected a BOM in the synthetic JUnit runner before any test execution. Original runner/log retained; BOM-only fix then javac/JUnit4 passed.",
    "First external Java first4 sessions passed; fifth original-traditional unowned createSession was correctly refused by existing admission, before browser execution. Vector corrected to fifth admitted owned Await-unsupported session; only isolated external Java recompiled/reran, not Kotlin/JUnit4."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Browser compatibility remains incomplete: only finite legacy SourceLoginJsExtensions startBrowser nonawait plain HTTP(S) GET is admitted in this slice.",
    "startBrowserAwait/finalURL+body/refetch, POST initial prefetch, explicit local HTML WebJS, showBrowser, general/V2 java=source browser methods remain explicitly unsupported/unported.",
    "The reused browser UI has no sourceRunHandler and installs no legacy source/JSC bridge. Its future Cookie capture stays under existing browser/CookieStore owner and is not a completed Cookie effect of the producer.",
    "Existing single-sheet queue differs from Android independent concurrent Activity opening. Waiting/presentation deadline and bounded URL/header representability limits remain embedding boundaries.",
    "Source revision checks use existing current binding/revocation snapshots, not an atomic transaction with arbitrary later source-store removal.",
    "overFullScreen preserves underlying views per UIKit docs; actual SwiftUI parent onDisappear, transitions, cancellation, WK navigation and Cookie behavior still require SDK/device execution.",
    "Authored Native1 now uses real shared process/JNI/default UIKit Presenter and awaits actual dismissal, retaining all Root10 prior methods/Fixture. It has NOT run.",
    "Only grammar checked Swift; no SDK/typechecking or actual Native test pass. Exact incremental JVM evidence must not be restated as fresh full Gradle compile."
